{%- comment -%}
  Size guide.

  Band and cup values are the product's real Shopify option values — the
  theme never invents a size. Measurements come only from what the merchant
  supplies: a `size_measurements` line per size, or a product metafield when
  one is set. Where nothing is supplied the column simply stays empty rather
  than showing a fabricated number.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign band_option = null
  assign cup_option = null
  assign panty_option = null
  comment
    An option that names the cup can never be the band. "Cup size" contains
    the band keyword ("size"), so on the products where Shopify lists the cup
    option first it was being claimed as the band and both names ended up
    pointing at the same option — which put cup letters in the band column of
    the size guide. Deciding the cup first, and refusing it for the band,
    resolves every option order in the catalogue.
  endcomment
  comment
    A combo lists three size options — band, cup and the bottom half — and
    every one of them contains the band keyword ("size"). Cup and bottom are
    therefore decided first and refused for the band, exactly as the cup
    already was, so the band cannot swallow "Panty Size" on the sets where
    Shopify lists it before the bra size.
  endcomment
  assign panty_keyword = section.settings.panty_option_name | default: 'panty'
  for option in product.options_with_values
    assign lower_name = option.name | downcase
    assign option_is_cup = false
    assign option_is_panty = false
    if lower_name contains section.settings.cup_option_name
      assign option_is_cup = true
    endif
    if lower_name contains panty_keyword
      assign option_is_panty = true
    endif
    if cup_option == null and option_is_cup
      assign cup_option = option
    endif
    if panty_option == null and option_is_panty
      assign panty_option = option
    endif
    if band_option == null and option_is_cup == false and option_is_panty == false and lower_name contains section.settings.band_option_name
      assign band_option = option
    endif
  endfor

  assign measurement_lines = section.settings.size_measurements | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
  assign metafield_chart = product.metafields.custom.size_chart
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Which size chart belongs to this product.

  Detection uses the product's own Shopify classification only — product
  type, standard category, tags and the optional custom.size_chart_type
  metafield. The product title is deliberately not matched, so a combo or
  bundle never inherits a chart from a word in its name. Each `size_chart`
  block carries its own keywords, so the merchant decides in the Theme
  Editor which products get which chart; blocks are tested in editor order
  and the first match wins. A block with no keywords is the fallback for
  products nothing else matches, and when no block matches at all the
  section-level chart settings are used, so existing setups keep working.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign chart_haystack = product.type
  if product.category != blank
    assign chart_haystack = chart_haystack | append: ' | ' | append: product.category.name
  endif
  if product.metafields.custom.size_chart_type != blank
    assign chart_haystack = chart_haystack | append: ' | ' | append: product.metafields.custom.size_chart_type
  endif
  for tag in product.tags
    assign chart_haystack = chart_haystack | append: ' | ' | append: tag
  endfor
  assign chart_haystack = chart_haystack | downcase

  comment
    Two haystacks, because the two keyword lists answer different questions.

    The size option names are Shopify data as much as the type and the tags
    are, and on a catalogue where type, category and tags have not been
    filled in they are the only classification a product carries: an option
    called "Cup Size" is evidence of a bra, "Panty Size" of a brief. So the
    match keywords are tested against the option names too.

    The exclude keywords are not. They exist to keep a brief from being
    handed bra measurements, and a set legitimately offers both kinds of
    size — testing "panty" against a combo's own option names would refuse
    it the bra chart it needs. Exclusion stays a judgement about what the
    product is, which is what type, category and tags describe.
  endcomment
  assign chart_option_haystack = chart_haystack
  for option in product.options_with_values
    assign chart_option_haystack = chart_option_haystack | append: ' | ' | append: option.name
  endfor
  assign chart_option_haystack = chart_option_haystack | downcase

  assign chart_block = null
  assign chart_fallback = null
  assign panty_chart_block = null
  assign panty_chart_matched = false
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.type != 'size_chart'
      continue
    endif
    comment
      Every block is run through the same keyword test; only where the answer
      is filed differs. A chart marked as bottom sizing is held aside so a set
      can show it alongside its top chart, and so a brief classified by type
      or tag alone still finds it even when its size option is called plain
      Size and nothing else.
    endcomment
    assign chart_excluded = false
    assign exclude_words = block.settings.exclude | downcase | split: ','
    for word in exclude_words
      assign word = word | strip
      if word != blank and chart_haystack contains word
        assign chart_excluded = true
      endif
    endfor

    assign chart_matched = false
    if chart_excluded == false and block.settings.match != blank
      assign match_words = block.settings.match | downcase | split: ','
      for word in match_words
        assign word = word | strip
        if word != blank and chart_option_haystack contains word
          assign chart_matched = true
        endif
      endfor
    endif

    comment
      Shopify validates a JSON template against the section schema it already
      holds, so on the upload that introduces chart_scope the setting can be
      dropped from the template before the new schema lands. Falling back to
      the block's own keywords means a chart written for the bottom half is
      still recognised as one, and the guide cannot quietly lose it.
    endcomment
    assign block_is_bottom = false
    if block.settings.chart_scope == 'bottom'
      assign block_is_bottom = true
    elsif block.settings.chart_scope == blank and block.settings.match contains panty_keyword
      assign block_is_bottom = true
    endif

    if block_is_bottom
      if panty_chart_block == null
        assign panty_chart_block = block
        assign panty_chart_matched = chart_matched
      endif
      continue
    endif
    if block.settings.match == blank
      if chart_fallback == null
        assign chart_fallback = block
      endif
      continue
    endif
    if chart_block == null and chart_matched
      assign chart_block = block
    endif
  endfor
  if chart_block == null
    assign chart_block = chart_fallback
  endif

  assign chart_rows_raw = section.settings.size_chart_rows
  assign chart_columns_raw = section.settings.size_chart_columns
  assign chart_heading = section.settings.size_chart_heading | default: 'Size chart'
  assign chart_category = section.settings.size_chart_category
  assign measure_heading = section.settings.measure_heading | default: 'How to measure'
  assign measure_step_1_title = section.settings.measure_step_1_title
  assign measure_step_1 = section.settings.measure_step_1
  assign measure_step_2_title = section.settings.measure_step_2_title
  assign measure_step_2 = section.settings.measure_step_2
  assign between_sizes_heading = section.settings.between_sizes_heading | default: 'Between sizes?'
  assign between_sizes = section.settings.between_sizes
  assign size_note = section.settings.size_note
  assign size_contact = section.settings.size_contact

  comment
    The chart's own words — how to measure, what to do between sizes, the
    footnote — come from whichever block is actually describing this product.
    On a brief that is the bottom chart, which is never the top chart, so
    without this the measuring instructions the merchant wrote for it would
    be dropped along with it.
  endcomment
  assign guide_block = chart_block
  if guide_block == null and panty_chart_matched
    assign guide_block = panty_chart_block
  endif

  if chart_block != null and chart_block.settings.rows != blank
    assign chart_rows_raw = chart_block.settings.rows
    assign chart_columns_raw = chart_block.settings.columns | default: chart_columns_raw
    assign chart_heading = chart_block.settings.heading | default: chart_heading
    assign chart_category = chart_block.settings.category | default: chart_category
  endif

  if guide_block != null and guide_block.settings.rows != blank
    assign measure_heading = guide_block.settings.measure_heading | default: measure_heading
    if guide_block.settings.measure_step_1 != blank or guide_block.settings.measure_step_2 != blank
      assign measure_step_1_title = guide_block.settings.measure_step_1_title
      assign measure_step_1 = guide_block.settings.measure_step_1
      assign measure_step_2_title = guide_block.settings.measure_step_2_title
      assign measure_step_2 = guide_block.settings.measure_step_2
    endif
    assign between_sizes_heading = guide_block.settings.between_sizes_heading | default: between_sizes_heading
    assign between_sizes = guide_block.settings.between_sizes | default: between_sizes
    assign size_note = guide_block.settings.size_note | default: size_note
    assign size_contact = guide_block.settings.size_contact | default: size_contact
  endif

  assign selected_band = ''
  assign selected_cup = ''
  if band_option
    assign selected_band = band_option.selected_value.name | default: ''
  endif
  if cup_option
    assign selected_cup = cup_option.selected_value.name | default: ''
  endif
  assign current_code = selected_band | append: selected_cup | upcase | strip

  assign panty_rows = ''
  assign panty_columns = ''
  assign panty_heading = chart_heading
  assign panty_category = ''
  assign selected_panty = ''
  if panty_option
    assign selected_panty = panty_option.selected_value.name | default: ''
  endif
  if panty_chart_block
    assign panty_rows = panty_chart_block.settings.rows
    assign panty_columns = panty_chart_block.settings.columns
    assign panty_heading = panty_chart_block.settings.heading | default: chart_heading
    assign panty_category = panty_chart_block.settings.category
  endif

  comment
    Which halves of the body this product actually sizes.

    A Cup Size option is evidence of a top and a Panty Size option of a
    bottom, and a chart whose own keywords match the product is evidence
    either way — that is how a brief classified by type or tag is recognised
    when its size option is called plain "Size". A set has both and shows
    both. A product with neither shows whatever the old resolution produced,
    so a shop that classifies its products by type and tags is unaffected.
  endcomment
  assign has_top = false
  assign has_bottom = false
  if cup_option or chart_block
    assign has_top = true
  endif
  if panty_option or panty_chart_matched
    assign has_bottom = true
  endif

  assign show_top_chart = true
  if has_bottom and has_top == false
    assign show_top_chart = false
  endif

  assign show_bottom_chart = false
  if has_bottom and panty_rows != blank and panty_chart_block != chart_block
    assign show_bottom_chart = true
  endif

  comment
    Which size the bottom chart should mark as the shopper's own. On a set
    that is the bottom option; on a brief whose only option is called Size it
    is that one.
  endcomment
  if selected_panty == blank and has_bottom and panty_option == null and band_option
    assign selected_panty = band_option.selected_value.name | default: ''
  endif

  comment
    Whether the guide has any sizing in it at all. "Between sizes?" and
    the contact footnote are general advice, not sizing, so a product
    the charts do not cover was offering a Size guide link that opened
    a drawer telling the shopper nothing about their size. The link is
    only worth showing when there is something behind it.
  endcomment
  comment
    On a set both charts are on screen at once. Two blocks headed Size chart
    over a merchant category naming a different product, such as High-Waist
    Briefs on a lingerie set, does not tell the shopper which one to read.
    Labelling each chart with the option it sizes uses the exact words printed
    above the picker they just used, which are the product's own Shopify
    option names and nothing invented.
  endcomment
  assign shows_both_charts = false
  if show_top_chart and chart_rows_raw != blank and show_bottom_chart and panty_option
    assign shows_both_charts = true
  endif
  if shows_both_charts
    if band_option
      assign chart_category = band_option.name
    endif
    assign panty_category = panty_option.name
  endif

  assign guide_has_sizing = false
  if band_option and section.settings.size_measurements != blank
    assign guide_has_sizing = true
  endif
  if cup_option and chart_rows_raw == blank
    assign guide_has_sizing = true
  endif
  if metafield_chart != blank
    assign guide_has_sizing = true
  endif
  if show_top_chart and chart_rows_raw != blank
    assign guide_has_sizing = true
  endif
  if show_bottom_chart
    assign guide_has_sizing = true
  endif
-%}

<product-info
  id="MainProduct-{{ section.id }}"
  class="gy-pdp gy-section gy-section--ivory"
  style="--gy-pad-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px; --gy-pad-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;"
  data-section="{{ section.id }}"
  data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  data-update-url="true"
  data-url="{{ product.url }}"
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div class="gy-container gy-pdp__inner">
    <div class="gy-pdp__media">
      {%- render 'gy-product-gallery',
        product: product,
        section_id: section.id,
        zoom: section.settings.enable_zoom
      -%}
    </div>

    <div class="gy-pdp__info" id="ProductInfo-{{ section.id }}">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- case block.type -%}
          {%- when '@app' -%}
            <div class="gy-pdp__app" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{% render block %}</div>

          {%- when 'vendor' -%}
            {%- if product.vendor != blank -%}
              <p class="gy-pdp__vendor" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ product.vendor }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}

          {%- when 'title' -%}
            <h1 class="gy-pdp__title" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ product.title }}</h1>

          {%- when 'price' -%}
            <div class="gy-pdp__price-block" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <div id="price-{{ section.id }}" class="gy-pdp__price" role="status">
                {%- render 'price', product: product, use_variant: true, show_badges: false, price_class: 'price--large' -%}
              </div>

              <div class="gy-pdp__price-meta" id="PriceMeta-{{ section.id }}">
                {%- if compare_at > current_price -%}
                  <span class="gy-pdp__compare">
                    <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.product.price.regular_price' | t }}</span>
                    {%- if settings.currency_code_enabled -%}
                      {{ compare_at | money_with_currency }}
                    {%- else -%}
                      {{ compare_at | money }}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                  {%- if block.settings.show_saving and discount_percent > 0 -%}
                    <span class="gy-pdp__saving">
                      {{ 'sections.hero_product.discount_html' | t: percent: discount_percent }}
                    </span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if block.settings.show_tax_note -%}
                  <span class="gy-pdp__tax">{{ 'products.product.taxes_included' | t }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>

              <div
                id="Inventory-{{ section.id }}"
                class="gy-pdp__stock{% unless product.selected_or_first_available_variant.inventory_management == 'shopify' %} gy-pdp__stock--hidden{% endunless %}"
                role="status"
              >
                {%- if variant.available -%}
                  {%- if variant.inventory_management == 'shopify'
                    and variant.inventory_quantity > 0
                    and variant.inventory_quantity <= block.settings.inventory_threshold
                  -%}
                    {{ 'products.product.inventory_low_stock' | t }}
                  {%- else -%}
                    {{ 'products.product.inventory_in_stock' | t }}
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- else -%}
                  {{ 'products.product.inventory_out_of_stock' | t }}
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            </div>

          {%- when 'variant_picker' -%}
            <div class="gy-pdp__variants">
              <div class="gy-pdp__variants-head">
                <div>
                  {%- if block.settings.heading != blank -%}
                    <p class="gy-pdp__variants-title">{{ block.settings.heading | escape }}</p>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- if block.settings.subheading != blank -%}
                    <p class="gy-pdp__variants-sub">{{ block.settings.subheading | escape }}</p>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>

                {%- if block.settings.show_size_guide and guide_has_sizing -%}
                  <button class="gy-pdp__size-link" type="button" data-gy-size-guide-open aria-haspopup="dialog">
                    {{ section.settings.size_guide_label | default: 'Size guide' | escape }}
                    <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
                  </button>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>

              {%- render 'product-variant-picker',
                product: product,
                block: block,
                product_form_id: product_form_id
              -%}
            </div>

          {%- when 'quantity_selector' -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign cart_qty = cart | item_count_for_variant: variant.id
            -%}
            <div class="gy-pdp__quantity product-form__input product-form__quantity" id="Quantity-Form-{{ section.id }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <label class="quantity__label form__label" for="Quantity-{{ section.id }}">
                {{ 'products.product.quantity.label' | t }}
                <span class="quantity__rules-cart{% if cart_qty == 0 %} hidden{% endif %}">
                  {%- render 'loading-spinner' -%}
                  <span>({{ 'products.product.quantity.in_cart_html' | t: quantity: cart_qty }})</span>
                </span>
              </label>
              <quantity-input class="quantity" data-url="{{ product.url }}" data-section="{{ section.id }}">
                <button class="quantity__button" name="minus" type="button">
                  <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.product.quantity.decrease' | t: product: product.title | escape }}</span>
                  <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-minus.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
                </button>
                <input
                  class="quantity__input"
                  type="number"
                  name="quantity"
                  id="Quantity-{{ section.id }}"
                  data-cart-quantity="{{ cart_qty }}"
                  data-min="{{ variant.quantity_rule.min }}"
                  min="{{ variant.quantity_rule.min }}"
                  {% if variant.quantity_rule.max != null %}
                    data-max="{{ variant.quantity_rule.max }}"
                    max="{{ variant.quantity_rule.max }}"
                  {% endif %}
                  step="{{ variant.quantity_rule.increment }}"
                  value="{{ variant.quantity_rule.min }}"
                  form="{{ product_form_id }}"
                >
                <button class="quantity__button" name="plus" type="button">
                  <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.product.quantity.increase' | t: product: product.title | escape }}</span>
                  <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-plus.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
                </button>
              </quantity-input>
              <div class="quantity__rules caption" id="Quantity-Rules-{{ section.id }}"></div>
            </div>

          {%- when 'buy_buttons' -%}
            <div class="gy-pdp__buy" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              {%- render 'buy-buttons',
                block: block,
                product: product,
                product_form_id: product_form_id,
                section_id: section.id,
                show_pickup_availability: true
              -%}
            </div>

          {%- when 'highlights' -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Editorial presentation of the product's own Shopify description.
              The lines below are the merchant's own text split on the bullet
              glyphs already used in Admin — nothing is added or rewritten.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign source = product.description | replace: '<br>', '✔' | replace: '<br/>', '✔' | replace: '<br />', '✔'
              assign source = source | replace: '</p>', '✔' | replace: '</li>', '✔'
              assign source = source | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | replace: '&amp;', '&'
              assign source = source | replace: 'Product Description:', '' | replace: 'Product description:', ''
              assign source = source | replace: '✓', '✔' | replace: '•', '✔'
              assign lines = source | split: '✔'
            -%}
            {%- assign printed = 0 -%}
            <div class="gy-pdp__highlights" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              {%- if block.settings.heading != blank -%}
                <p class="gy-pdp__highlights-heading">{{ block.settings.heading | escape }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
              <ul role="list">
                {%- for line in lines -%}
                  {%- assign clean = line | strip -%}
                  {%- if clean != blank and clean.size > 2 and printed < block.settings.max_lines -%}
                    <li>{{ clean }}</li>
                    {%- assign printed = printed | plus: 1 -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            </div>

          {%- when 'short_description' -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign words = block.settings.words | default: 32
              assign short = product.description | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | replace: '&amp;', '&'
              assign short = short | replace: 'Product Description:', '' | replace: 'Product description:', ''
              assign short = short | replace: '✔', '' | replace: '✓', '' | replace: '•', ''
              assign short = short | strip | truncatewords: words
            -%}
            {%- if short != blank -%}
              <p class="gy-pdp__short" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ short }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}

          {%- when 'trust' -%}
            <ul class="gy-pdp__trust" role="list" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              {%- assign points = block.settings.points | split: '|' -%}
              {%- for point in points -%}
                <li>{{ point | strip }}</li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>

          {%- when 'details' -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign body = block.settings.content
              if block.settings.source == 'description' and product.description != blank
                assign body = product.description
              endif
            -%}
            {%- if body != blank -%}
              <details class="gy-pdp__accordion" {% if block.settings.open %}open{% endif %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <summary>
                  <span>{{ block.settings.heading | escape }}</span>
                  <span class="gy-pdp__accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                </summary>
                <div class="gy-pdp__accordion-body rte">{{ body }}</div>
              </details>
            {%- endif -%}
        {%- endcase -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- if guide_has_sizing -%}
  <div class="gy-pdp__drawer" data-gy-size-guide-drawer hidden>
    <div class="gy-pdp__drawer-scrim" data-gy-size-guide-close></div>
    <aside
      class="gy-pdp__drawer-panel"
      role="dialog"
      aria-modal="true"
      aria-labelledby="SizeGuideTitle-{{ section.id }}"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      <header class="gy-pdp__drawer-head">
        <div>
          <p class="gy-pdp__drawer-title" id="SizeGuideTitle-{{ section.id }}">
            {{ section.settings.size_guide_heading | default: 'Find your best fit.' | escape }}
          </p>
          {%- if section.settings.size_guide_intro != blank -%}
            <p class="gy-pdp__drawer-intro">{{ section.settings.size_guide_intro | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <button
          class="gy-pdp__drawer-close"
          type="button"
          data-gy-size-guide-close
          aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t }}"
        >
          &times;
        </button>
      </header>

      <div class="gy-pdp__drawer-body">
        {%- if band_option and section.settings.size_measurements != blank -%}
          <section class="gy-guide__block">
            <h3 class="gy-guide__label">{{ band_option.name }}</h3>
            <table class="gy-guide__table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">{{ band_option.name }}</th>
                  <th scope="col">{{ section.settings.measurement_label | default: 'Underbust' | escape }}</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {%- for value in band_option.values -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign measurement = ''
                    for line in measurement_lines
                      assign parts = line | strip | split: ':'
                      assign key = parts[0] | strip
                      if key == value.name and parts.size > 1
                        assign measurement = parts[1] | strip
                      endif
                    endfor
                  -%}
                  <tr {% if value.selected %}class="is-current"{% endif %}>
                    <th scope="row">{{ value.name }}</th>
                    <td>
                      {%- if measurement != blank -%}
                        {{ measurement }}
                      {%- else -%}
                        <span class="gy-guide__blank" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span>
                        <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'sections.gy.measurement_not_set' | t }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </section>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if cup_option and chart_rows_raw == blank -%}
          <section class="gy-guide__block">
            <h3 class="gy-guide__label">{{ cup_option.name }}</h3>
            <ul class="gy-guide__cups" role="list">
              {%- for value in cup_option.values -%}
                <li class="{% if value.selected %}is-current{% endif %}">{{ value.name }}</li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </section>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if metafield_chart != blank -%}
          <section class="gy-guide__block gy-guide__metafield rte">
            {{ metafield_chart | metafield_tag }}
          </section>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Size charts. A bra shows the top chart, a brief shows the bottom
          chart, and a set shows both — decided by the size options the product
          actually offers, so a combo is never left with only half its sizing.
        {%- endcomment -%}

        {%- if show_top_chart -%}
          {%- render 'gy-size-chart',
            heading: chart_heading,
            category: chart_category,
            columns: chart_columns_raw,
            rows: chart_rows_raw,
            current_code: current_code
          -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The bottom half of a set. It is rendered whenever the product offers
          a bottom size option and the merchant has published a bottom chart,
          which is what was missing on every combo: the guide resolved a single
          chart, so the panty sizes in the picker had nothing to read against.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if show_bottom_chart -%}
          {%- render 'gy-size-chart',
            heading: panty_heading,
            category: panty_category,
            columns: panty_columns,
            rows: panty_rows,
            current_code: selected_panty
          -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if measure_step_1 != blank or measure_step_2 != blank -%}
          <section class="gy-guide__block">
            <h3 class="gy-guide__label">{{ measure_heading | escape }}</h3>
            <ol class="gy-guide__steps" role="list">
              {%- if measure_step_1 != blank -%}
                <li>
                  <span class="gy-guide__step-number">01</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="gy-guide__step-title">{{ measure_step_1_title | escape }}</p>
                    <p class="gy-guide__step-text">{{ measure_step_1 | escape }}</p>
                  </div>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if measure_step_2 != blank -%}
                <li>
                  <span class="gy-guide__step-number">02</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="gy-guide__step-title">{{ measure_step_2_title | escape }}</p>
                    <p class="gy-guide__step-text">{{ measure_step_2 | escape }}</p>
                  </div>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
            </ol>
          </section>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if between_sizes != blank -%}
          <section class="gy-guide__block gy-guide__note">
            <h3 class="gy-guide__label">{{ between_sizes_heading | escape }}</h3>
            <p>{{ between_sizes | escape }}</p>
          </section>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if size_note != blank or size_contact != blank -%}
          <div class="gy-guide__footnote">
            {%- if size_note != blank -%}
              <p>{{ size_note | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if size_contact != blank -%}
              <p>{{ size_contact | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.size_guide_text != blank -%}
          <div class="gy-guide__block rte">{{ section.settings.size_guide_text }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if section.settings.enable_sticky_bar -%}
    <div class="gy-pdp__sticky" data-gy-sticky-bar hidden>
      <div class="gy-pdp__sticky-inner">
        {%- comment -%}
          The selected variant's own image where Shopify has one, so the bar
          shows the piece in the colour being bought rather than the product's
          default photograph.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign sticky_image = variant.featured_media.preview_image | default: product.featured_image
        -%}
        <div class="gy-pdp__sticky-media">
          {%- if sticky_image -%}
            <img
              src="{{ sticky_image | image_url: width: 120 }}"
              width="{{ sticky_image.width }}"
              height="{{ sticky_image.height }}"
              alt=""
              loading="lazy"
            >
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <div class="gy-pdp__sticky-text">
          <p class="gy-pdp__sticky-title">{{ product.title }}</p>
          {%- comment -%}
            A div, not a p: snippets/price.liquid renders a div, and a div
            inside a paragraph makes the browser close the paragraph early —
            which left this wrapper empty, put the price outside it, and so
            stopped both of its style rules from ever matching. That is why
            the struck compare-at price was showing in the bar.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="gy-pdp__sticky-price" id="StickyPrice-{{ section.id }}">
            {%- render 'price', product: product, use_variant: true -%}
          </div>
        </div>
        <button class="gy-button gy-pdp__sticky-button" type="button" data-gy-sticky-add>
          {{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</product-info>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "GentleYou product",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "gy-pdp-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Gallery" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enable_zoom", "label": "Open the active image full size on click", "default": true },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Size guide" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "size_guide_label", "label": "Trigger label", "default": "Size guide" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "size_guide_heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Find your best fit." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "size_guide_intro", "label": "Supporting line", "default": "Simple measurements to help you choose comfortably." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "band_option_name", "label": "Band option name contains", "info": "Which product option holds the band size. Lower case.", "default": "size" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cup_option_name", "label": "Cup option name contains", "info": "Which product option holds the cup size. Lower case.", "default": "cup" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "panty_option_name", "label": "Bottom option name contains", "info": "Which product option holds the panty or brief size. Lower case.", "default": "panty" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "measurement_label", "label": "Measurement column heading", "default": "Underbust" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "size_measurements", "label": "Measurements", "info": "One per line as \"size: measurement\", for example \"32: 68-72 cm\". Sizes with nothing here show an empty cell — the theme never invents a measurement. A product metafield custom.size_chart is also rendered when set." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "size_chart_heading", "label": "Size chart heading", "default": "Size chart" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "size_chart_category", "label": "Size chart category", "default": "Bras" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "size_chart_columns", "label": "Size chart column headings", "info": "Separated by |.", "default": "Size|Underbust (inch)|Bust (inch)|UK size|EU size" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "size_chart_rows", "label": "Size chart rows", "info": "One row per line, columns separated by |. The first column is matched against the selected band and cup to highlight a row." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "measure_heading", "label": "How to measure heading", "default": "How to measure" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "measure_step_1_title", "label": "Step 1 title", "default": "Measure your band" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "measure_step_1", "label": "Step 1 text", "default": "Wrap the measuring tape firmly around your ribcage, directly underneath your bust." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "measure_step_2_title", "label": "Step 2 title", "default": "Measure your bust" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "measure_step_2", "label": "Step 2 text", "default": "Measure around the fullest part of your bust without pulling the tape too tightly." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "between_sizes_heading", "label": "Between sizes heading", "default": "Between sizes?" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "between_sizes", "label": "Between sizes text", "default": "If you're between sizes, we recommend choosing the larger size for a more comfortable everyday fit." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "size_note", "label": "Size note", "default": "Fit can vary slightly by style and fabric. Please check the available options on the product page before ordering." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "size_contact", "label": "Help line", "info": "Optional. Shown under the size note." },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "size_guide_text", "label": "Extra content", "info": "Optional. Appears at the end of the panel." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Mobile" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enable_sticky_bar", "label": "Sticky purchase bar on mobile", "default": true },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Spacing" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding_top", "min": 0, "max": 120, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "label": "Top padding", "default": 48 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding_bottom", "min": 0, "max": 120, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "label": "Bottom padding", "default": 72 }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "@app" },
    { "type": "vendor", "name": "Vendor", "limit": 1 },
    { "type": "title", "name": "Title", "limit": 1 },
    {
      "type": "price", "name": "Price", "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_saving", "label": "Show saving percentage", "default": true },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_tax_note", "label": "Show tax note", "default": false },
        { "type": "range", "id": "inventory_threshold", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1, "label": "Low stock threshold", "default": 10 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "highlights", "name": "Highlights", "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Lists the product's own Shopify description, split on the bullets already used in Admin. Nothing is written by the theme." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Why you'll love it" },
        { "type": "range", "id": "max_lines", "min": 2, "max": 10, "step": 1, "label": "Maximum lines", "default": 6 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "short_description", "name": "Short description", "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Uses the product's own Shopify description, shortened." },
        { "type": "range", "id": "words", "min": 12, "max": 60, "step": 2, "label": "Words", "default": 32 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "variant_picker", "name": "Variant picker", "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "select", "id": "picker_type", "label": "Style", "default": "button",
          "options": [ { "value": "dropdown", "label": "Dropdown" }, { "value": "button", "label": "Pills" } ]
        },
        {
          "type": "select", "id": "swatch_shape", "label": "Swatch shape", "default": "circle",
          "options": [ { "value": "circle", "label": "Circle" }, { "value": "square", "label": "Square" }, { "value": "none", "label": "None" } ]
        },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_size_guide", "label": "Show size guide link", "default": true },
        { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading above options", "default": "Find your fit." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "subheading", "label": "Small line under the heading", "default": "Choose your size, cup & colour." }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "quantity_selector", "name": "Quantity selector", "limit": 1 },
    {
      "type": "buy_buttons", "name": "Buy buttons", "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_dynamic_checkout", "label": "Show dynamic checkout buttons", "default": true },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_gift_card_recipient", "label": "Show gift card recipient form", "default": true }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "trust", "name": "Reassurance line", "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "points", "label": "Points", "info": "Separate with |. Use the store's own published policy wording.", "default": "Cash on delivery | Free prepaid shipping | 3-day size exchange" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "size_chart", "name": "Size chart",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Shown inside the size guide only when this product matches the keywords below. Keywords are checked against the product's Shopify type, category, tags, size option names and the custom.size_chart_type metafield \u2014 never its title \u2014 so combos and bundles do not pick up a chart by accident. Blocks are checked in the order they appear here and the first match wins. Leave the keywords empty to make this the chart for products nothing else matches." },
        { "type": "select", "id": "chart_scope", "label": "This chart sizes", "info": "A set that offers both a bra size and a panty size shows its top chart and its bottom chart together.", "default": "top", "options": [ { "value": "top", "label": "The top \u2014 bra, bralette, nightwear" }, { "value": "bottom", "label": "The bottom \u2014 panty, brief" } ] },
        { "type": "text", "id": "match", "label": "Show when type, category or tags contain", "info": "Separated by commas, for example: panty, panties, brief, briefs." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "exclude", "label": "But never when they contain", "info": "Optional. Separated by commas, for example: combo, set." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Size chart" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "category", "label": "Product type label", "info": "Shown under the heading, for example \"High-Waist Briefs\"." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "columns", "label": "Column headings", "info": "Separated by |.", "default": "Size|Waist (inch)|Hip (inch)|UK size|EU size" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "rows", "label": "Rows", "info": "One row per line, columns separated by |. Enter the measurements exactly as published \u2014 the theme never converts or derives a number. The first column is matched against the selected size to highlight a row." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "measure_heading", "label": "How to measure heading", "default": "How to measure" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "measure_step_1_title", "label": "Step 1 title" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "measure_step_1", "label": "Step 1 text" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "measure_step_2_title", "label": "Step 2 title" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "measure_step_2", "label": "Step 2 text" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "between_sizes_heading", "label": "Between sizes heading", "default": "Between sizes?" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "between_sizes", "label": "Between sizes text" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "size_note", "label": "Size note" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "size_contact", "label": "Help line" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "details", "name": "Details section",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Description" },
        {
          "type": "select", "id": "source", "label": "Content", "default": "custom",
          "options": [ { "value": "description", "label": "Product description from Shopify" }, { "value": "custom", "label": "Text below" } ]
        },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "content", "label": "Text" },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "open", "label": "Open by default", "default": false }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "GentleYou product",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "vendor" }, { "type": "title" }, { "type": "price" },
        { "type": "short_description" }, { "type": "variant_picker" },
        { "type": "quantity_selector" }, { "type": "buy_buttons" }, { "type": "trust" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "enabled_on": { "templates": ["product"] }
}
{% endschema %}
